# Performance and motion

Budget: JS on home < 30KB gz. LCP = one hero image, `fetchpriority="high"`, never lazy. Everything below-fold lazy.

## Do

- Astro static HTML. CSS tokens, no runtime UI kit.
- Self-host 2 WOFF2 files, `preload`, `font-display: swap`, subset Latin.
- `<Image />` → AVIF/WebP, `sizes`, width/height set (no CLS).
- `content-visibility: auto` on below-fold sections.
- Motion: CSS opacity + 8–16px translate, 180–400ms. Hero scale max 1.03.

## Do not

- AOS, WOW, GSAP, jQuery, Nivo, Owl, Bootstrap, autoplay video, hero carousel.
- Animate `top`, `left`, `width`, `height`.
- Animate every card. One reveal per section, once.

```css
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  *, *::before, *::after {
    animation: none !important;
    transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;
  }
}
```

Reveal = ~20 lines of IntersectionObserver as an Astro island `client:visible`. If CSS-only is enough, skip JS.
